<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44306" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκρᾱτος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκρητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεράννυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-tempered, temperate</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				772
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκέφαλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				56
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					371d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>GA</u>
					752b30
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκρατον ποιεῖ τὴν θερμότητα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>PA</u>
					652b26
				</span></i>
			; of countries, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.Med.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				9.12.5
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκήσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					34.1.8
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; of the <i>temperate</i> zone, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.195
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεῖξις</span> Chrysipp.ib.<i><span class="en">
				219
			</span></i>; of liquids, <i>tempered, lukewarm</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(1).1390.108
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Andania</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.101
			</span></i>, etc.; of wine, <i>mixed for drinking</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				874a28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>temperate, mild</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλιγαρχία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1320b21
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ. τοῦ ἤθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					1.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.208
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Antip.Thess.
			</span></i>): in Astrol., of beneficent planetary in fluences, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.911
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in Lit.
			Crit., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. ἁρμονία, ἑρμηνεία</span>,
				<i>mixed</i> style, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				21
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοινή</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Dem.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνθήκη ὀνομάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
					46
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκρητοι πρὸς ἅπαντας</span> (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκράς</span> (A) <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Decent.</u>
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
			<i>temperately</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρείως καὶ
			εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1251.14
			</span></i>; <i>temperately</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				1.342
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἔχειν</span> to be
			<i>temperate</i>, of climate, <i><span class="en">
				Cleom.
				1.2
			</span></i>; to be <i>lukewarm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				1.64
			</span></i>.</div>
